        "subject": "LU-19536 tests: race mprotect with an unaligned DIO write",
        "message": "LU-19536 tests: race mprotect with an unaligned DIO write\n\nAdd sanity test_119y and its helper dio_mprotect_race, which\nmakes the tail of the user buffer of an unaligned DIO write\nPROT_NONE from another thread while the write is in flight.\nThe write may fail, but it must never report as written\ndata it did not copy from the user buffer.\n\nThe window between the up front fault-in and the end of the\ncopy depends on the node, so unless given a delay the helper\ntimes an uncontended write first and sweeps the delays over\nthat time. Without the fix for short copies, 18 of 400 such\nwrites on a VM reported success without copying all of\ntheir data.\n\nThe helper is based on a reproducer by Andrew Perepechko.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity env=ONLY=119y,ONLY_REPEAT=10\nReported-by: Andrew Perepechko <andrew.perepechko@hpe.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I78beb88cb5e00ce4cf6c69e059fa6b33131af9a6\n"
      },
